(* Variant mimic-link: the mimic path, as the code has it, against an attacker that holds the link of alice: the public key
   of the server and her short id (AUD-7, #425). A client of the server holds them, and so does anyone who reads the link,
   which is typed by hand into the MimicClient setting today. The attacker gets the temporary certificate of the server and
   learns that it is no decoy, but it cannot answer alice as the server: that takes the auth key of her ClientHello. *)

process
  ( Setup()
  | MimicSetup()
  | LeakLinkShortId()
  | MimicSessions(bt_export, kp_on)
  )
